{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>That it may go well with you and that your days be long.</b> In the matter of sending away the nest there is a certain bestowal of kindness toward the public — not to destroy the offspring of the birds of the field, which are ownerless — and this pertains to sending away the mother. He says that even for this small measure of kindness, one enjoys the fruit in this world while the principal endures for the world to come."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:58.198097766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}